{"source_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001221", "source_dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_subset": null, "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "source_original_index": 1221, "source_question": "n 1931, Barbara McClintock discovered that genes could change position on a chromosome. In corn plants, if a certain gene was moved next to the gene that controls kernel color, the kernels in an ear of corn were various colors. Which statement best supports McClintock's discovery?", "source_choices": ["Genes control inherited traits in organisms.", "Corn plants can reproduce in laboratory environments.", "Chromosomes can move around in the nucleus of a cell.", "Genes are able to disappear and reappear in later generations."], "source_answer": "Genes control inherited traits in organisms.", "candidate_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001221", "source_snapshot": {"dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "original_index": 1221, "record": {"question": "n 1931, Barbara McClintock discovered that genes could change position on a chromosome. In corn plants, if a certain gene was moved next to the gene that controls kernel color, the kernels in an ear of corn were various colors. Which statement best supports McClintock's discovery?", "choices": ["Genes control inherited traits in organisms.", "Corn plants can reproduce in laboratory environments.", "Chromosomes can move around in the nucleus of a cell.", "Genes are able to disappear and reappear in later generations."], "answer": "Genes control inherited traits in organisms.", "source": "ai2_arc"}}, "created_at": "2026-08-09T14:33:00.703231+00:00", "extraction": {"model": "qwen3.7-plus", "role": "TRIPLE_LABEL_MODEL", "prompt_version": "atomic-factual-triple-v6", "temperature": 0.0, "api_model": "qwen3.7-flash-2026-07-15", "raw_response": null, "attempt_count": 1, "error": {"