{"source_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001319", "source_dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_subset": null, "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "source_original_index": 1319, "source_question": "Use The Periodic Table of the Elements and the information below to answer the question. Magnesium metal (Mg) is grayish-white in color and reacts actively with water. Fluorine (F2) is a greenish-yellow gas at room temperature and is a member of the halogen family. These two elements react to produce magnesium fluoride (MgF2), a chemical commonly used in making windows and lenses. According to the Periodic Table of the Elements, which element is most similar to magnesium (Mg)?", "source_choices": ["calcium (Ca)", "iodine (I)", "sodium (Na)", "sulfur (S)"], "source_answer": "calcium (Ca)", "candidate_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001319", "source_snapshot": {"dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "original_index": 1319, "record": {"question": "Use The Periodic Table of the Elements and the information below to answer the question. Magnesium metal (Mg) is grayish-white in color and reacts actively with water. Fluorine (F2) is a greenish-yellow gas at room temperature and is a member of the halogen family. These two elements react to produce magnesium fluoride (MgF2), a chemical commonly used in making windows and lenses. According to the Periodic Table of the Elements, which element is most similar to magnesium (Mg)?", "choices": ["calcium (Ca)", "iodine (I)", "sodium (Na)", "sulfur (S)"], "answer": "calcium (Ca)", "source": "ai2_arc"}}, "created_at": "2026-08-09T14:33:19.747165+00:00", "extraction": {"model": "qwen3.7-plus", "role": "TRIPLE_LABEL_MODEL", "prompt_version": "atomic-factual-triple-v6", "temperature": 0.0, "api_model": "qwen3.7-flash-2026-07-15", "raw_response": null, "attempt_count": 1, "error": {"ca