{"source_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001425", "source_dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_subset": null, "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "source_original_index": 1425, "source_question": "The early Greeks are credited with many valid concepts in astronomy. Some of their theories were correct; some were later proven incorrect. One theory was that Earth was the center of the universe and that other planets circled Earth. The Greeks thought Earth did not move because its movement was not obvious from the surface of the planet. The Greeks also believed that an invisible sphere surrounding our planet contained the stars. This sphere rotated, explaining the apparent movement of constellations over time. Early Greeks also developed theories about the relationship between the moon and Earth. Why is the same side of the moon always visible from Earth?", "source_choices": ["The far side of the moon does not reflect sunlight.", "The moon stays in one location while Earth revolves around it.", "The period of rotation and the period of revolution for the moon are about the same.", "The moon rotates clockwise on its axis while Earth rotates counterclockwise on its axis."], "source_answer": "The period of rotation and the period of revolution for the moon are about the same.", "candidate_id": "raw_ai2_arc_easy_001425", "source_snapshot": {"dataset": "ai2_arc_easy", "source_path": "/Users/qiqing/learn_resource/mutil-language/pitfalls-cross-lingual/data/source/ai2_arc_easy.json", "original_index": 1425, "record": {"question": "The early Greeks are credited with many valid concepts in astronomy. Some of their theories were correct; some were later proven incorrect. One theory was that Earth was the center of the universe and that other planets circled Earth. The Greeks thought Earth did not move because its movement was not obvious from the surface of the planet. The Greeks also believed that an invisible sphere surrounding our planet contained the stars. This sphere rotated, explaining the apparent movement of constellations over time. Early Greeks also developed theories about the relationship between the moon and Earth. Why is the same side of the moon always visible from Earth?", "choices": ["The far side of the moon does not reflect sunlight.", "The moon stays in one location while Earth revolves around it.", "The period of rotation and the period of revolution for the moon are about the same.", "The moon rotates clockwise on its axis while Earth rotates counterclockwise on its axis."], "answer": "The period of rotation and the period of revolution for the moon are about the same.", "source": "ai2_arc"}}, "created_at": "2026-08-09T14:33:40.974469+00:00", "extraction": {"model": "qwen3.7-plus", "role": "TRIPLE_LABEL_MODEL", "prompt_version": "atomic-factual-triple-v6", "temperature": 0.0, "api_model": "qwen3.7-flash-2026-07-15", "raw_response": null, "attempt_count": 1, "error": {"category": "permanent_failure", "message": "Error code: 403 - {'error': {'message': 'Free quota exhausted. To continue accessing the model on a paid basis, please add funds or disable the \"use free tier only\" mode in the management console.', 'type': 'AllocationQuota.FreeTierOnly', 'param': None, 'code': 'AllocationQuota.FreeTierOnly'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-c3edc769-2db8-90a8-89ed-127129f4174f', 'request_id': 'c3edc769-2db8-90a8-89ed-127129f4174f'}"}}, "terminal_status": "extraction_failed", "extraction_status": null, "exclusion_reason": null, "subject": null, "subject_type": null, "relation_raw": null, "answer": null, "answer_type": null, "canonical_fact": null, "extraction_confidence": null, "parsed_response": null, "validation_errors": ["extraction_request_failed"], "retry_history": [{"terminal_status": "extraction_failed", "created_at": "2026-08-09T07:15:44.161015+00:00", "error": {"category": "permanent_failure", "message": "Error code: 403 - {'error': {'message': '预扣费额度失败, 用户剩余额度: ¥0.00